nrgchain - tridiagonalisation code for determining the tight-bidning
coefficients of the Wilson chain for NRG calculations

nrgchain determines the coefficients xi (hopping constants) and zeta
(on-site energies) for a Wilson chain. It takes the output from adapt
as its input.


Usage: nrgchain [options] [s|l] [parameter_file]

Option "-v" writes the resolved configuration and verbose diagnostics to
standard error; "-vv" increases verbosity further. "-V" and "--version" print
the project version and exit immediately. "-h" and "--help" print help.

The parameter file defaults to "param". Mode "s" calculates and saves the
intermediate tables without tridiagonalising; mode "l" loads those tables and
tridiagonalises them. A command-line mode overrides the corresponding settings
from the parameter file.

The parameter "nrgchain_tridiag" controls whether tridiagonalisation is
performed when no command-line mode overrides it.

Consult test/tools/nrgchain/nrgchain1/param for a sample parameter file.
